---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PAGINE, TESTI } from '../../i18n';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const t = TESTI[lang];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Filippo Cassi · Closer & Account Manager"
  description="Art, real estate, training. Every industry taught me a piece of the same craft: building trust."
  lang={lang}
  translations={PAGINE.chiSono}
>
  <section class="fc-hero compact">
    <img
      class="fc-face"
      src="/img/filippo-cassi-closer.jpg"
      alt="Filippo Cassi"
      width="480"
      height="480"
    />
    <div class="fc-over">About</div>
    <h1 class="fc-h1">
      Twelve years in sales,<br />
      three different worlds.
    </h1>
    <p>
      Art, real estate, training. Every industry taught me a piece of the same
      craft: building trust.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="fc-sec">
    <div class="fc-kick">The path</div>
    <h2>My story</h2>

    <ul class="fc-tl">
      <li>
        <span class="yr">2012 – 2014 · Pavia</span>
        <h3>Liguri Undici art gallery</h3>
        <p>
          My first steps in sales, surrounded by art. Nobody
          &ldquo;needs&rdquo; a painting: that is where I discovered that selling
          means telling stories and connecting people to a meaning, with passion
          and emotion.
        </p>
        <img
          class="fc-tl-photo"
          src="/img/filippo-cassi-galleria-arte-liguri-undici.jpg"
          alt="Filippo Cassi at the Liguri Undici art gallery in Pavia, with local institutional figures"
          loading="lazy"
          width="800"
          height="523"
        />
        <div class="fc-tl-cap">At the gallery, with local institutional figures.</div>
      </li>

      <li>
        <span class="yr">2014 – 2022 · Pavia</span>
        <h3>Tecnocasa — from agent to branch manager</h3>
        <p>
          The longest and most formative experience. In 2015 the results and the
          ability to lead others made me branch manager: under my management the
          office won regional and provincial awards and became a reference point
          in the area.
        </p>
        <div class="fc-tl-grid">
          <figure>
            <img
              src="/img/filippo-cassi-premio-miglior-agente-pavia.jpg"
              alt="Filippo Cassi awarded best estate agent by number of sales, province of Pavia"
              loading="lazy"
              width="700"
              height="525"
            />
            <figcaption class="fc-tl-cap">
              Awarded best agent by number of sales, province of Pavia
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img
              src="/img/filippo-cassi-pranzo-oreste-pasquali-tecnocasa.jpg"
              alt="Filippo Cassi at lunch with Oreste Pasquali, founding chairman of Tecnocasa"
              loading="lazy"
              width="700"
              height="393"
            />
            <figcaption class="fc-tl-cap">
              With Oreste Pasquali, founding chairman of Tecnocasa
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img
              src="/img/filippo-cassi-responsabile-agenzia-tecnocasa.jpg"
              alt="Filippo Cassi on the day of his promotion to Tecnocasa Branch Manager"
              loading="lazy"
              width="700"
              height="393"
            />
            <figcaption class="fc-tl-cap">
              The day of the promotion to Branch Manager
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img
              src="/img/filippo-cassi-premio-team-lombardia-tecnocasa.jpg"
              alt="Filippo Cassi's team awarded for revenue and sales, Lombardy region"
              loading="lazy"
              width="700"
              height="685"
            />
            <figcaption class="fc-tl-cap">
              My team awarded for revenue and sales, Lombardy region
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li>
        <span class="yr">2022 – 2024 · Las Palmas de Gran Canaria</span>
        <h3>The leap: new life, new skills</h3>
        <p>
          I started from scratch in the Canary Islands. A Master's in Digital
          Marketing (Digital Coach) and remote work as an appointment setter and
          closer for Unger Academy: daily phone contact with clients, managing
          appointments, supporting people through their training programmes.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <span class="yr">2024 – 2025 · Las Palmas de Gran Canaria</span>
        <div class="fc-tl-side">
          <div class="txt">
            <h3>Gilmar Canarias — international real estate consultant</h3>
            <p>
              I guide clients from all over the world in finding their ideal
              home. Every sale is not a transaction but a tailored journey:
              negotiation, empathy and building trust.
            </p>
          </div>
          <img
            src="/img/filippo-cassi-gilmar-canarias-ritratto.jpg"
            alt="Filippo Cassi, Gilmar Canarias real estate consultant"
            loading="lazy"
            width="500"
            height="500"
          />
        </div>
      </li>

      <li>
        <span class="yr">Today · Remote</span>
        <div class="fc-tl-side">
          <div class="txt">
            <h3>Unger Academy — Closer &amp; Account Manager</h3>
            <p>
              I qualify inbound leads with a focus on the appointments most
              likely to close, and work on improving funnel quality and the
              sales team's conversion rate.
            </p>
          </div>
          <img
            src="/img/filippo-cassi-oggi-unger.jpg"
            alt="Filippo Cassi today, Unger Academy"
            loading="lazy"
            width="500"
            height="500"
          />
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="fc-band">
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        &ldquo;When you understand the client's problem better than they do,<br />
        you no longer have to convince them: they ask you to lead the way.&rdquo;
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section class="fc-sec">
    <div class="fc-split">
      <div>
        <div class="fc-kick">Philosophy</div>
        <h2>How I work</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          I don't believe in external pressure: discounts expiring tonight,
          invented urgency. A client pushed into signing that way is deciding for
          somebody else's reasons, and it shows at the first difficulty. The
          pressure that works is internal: it comes when the client sees clearly
          where they are today, with real numbers, where they want to get to, and
          what every month of standing still is costing them. At that point there
          is no need to push: staying put has become more expensive than
          deciding.
        </p>
        <p>
          On a call I have only two jobs: to work out whether I can genuinely
          help the person in front of me, and to take every objection off the
          table before we talk about signing. Behind every objection there is an
          unanswered question — the price, the timing, the doubt about being able
          to do it — and my job is to bring it out and answer it, until choosing
          becomes the easiest thing. Empathy is not weakness: precisely because I
          have genuinely understood the client's situation, I can afford to be
          direct. And conviction cannot be acted: it comes through in the voice
          before it reaches the words.
        </p>
        <div class="fc-langs">
          <span>🇮🇹 Italiano — native</span>
          <span>🇪🇸 Español — advanced</span>
          <span>🇬🇧 English — advanced</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fc-cta">
    <h2>Let's talk.</h2>
    <p>
      I'm looking for opportunities as a closer and account manager, remote, in
      Italian, Spanish and English.
    </p>
    <p class="fc-actions">
      <a class="fc-btn" href={PAGINE.contatti[lang]}>{t.ctaContatto}</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
